# Your Product Name — Design System

> **For AI agents:** read this file completely before generating or modifying any UI component. Every color, spacing, radius, and type value used in generated code must come from the tokens above — never invent a new hex code or arbitrary pixel value. If a component needs a token that isn't defined here, ask before approximating one.

## Design Intent

Describe the aesthetic direction in 2-3 sentences. What should this product *feel* like? (e.g., "Confident and dense — built for expert users making fast decisions across a lot of data. Not playful, not minimal-for-minimalism's-sake.")

## Color Usage Rules

- `primary` — primary CTAs, active nav states, focus rings, links. Nowhere else.
- `secondary` — supporting/outline buttons, secondary actions.
- Semantic colors (`success`/`warning`/`error`/`info`) are reserved for their exact meaning — never repurpose `error` red for a decorative accent.
- Never introduce a color not listed above without updating this file first.

## Typography Usage

- Body text never smaller than `sm` (0.875rem / 14px); prefer `base` (16px) for primary reading content.
- Headings: `3xl`/Bold → page title, `2xl`/Bold → section title, `xl`/Semibold → subsection, `lg`/Semibold → card title.
- Max 3 weights in any single view.

## Spacing Rules

- All padding/margin/gap values must come from the spacing scale — never arbitrary values like `13px` or `22px`.
- Section padding: 32–64px vertical on desktop, 16–24px on mobile.

## Component Conventions

- Every interactive component implements: default, hover, focus-visible, active, disabled states.
- Icon-only buttons require `aria-label`.
- Destructive actions require a confirmation step.
- Loading states use skeletons for content-heavy views, not just a spinner.

## Constraints (Do Not Violate)

- Do not use colors outside the defined palette.
- Do not hardcode pixel values — always reference the token scale.
- Do not remove text labels from primary actions for a "cleaner" look — this measurably hurts usability (see `01-design-principles/design-principles.md` in the ui-ux-design knowledge base for the research behind this).
- Do not skip accessibility attributes (contrast, aria-labels, keyboard nav) to save time.

